  Drive aggregates (drive_repo.go, energy_repo.go, trip_repo.go) — SQL converts distance_m / 1609.344
                                           AS distance_mi; max_speed_mps / 0.44704 AS max_speed_mph.
                                           These DRIVE fields remain in mi/mph after the SQL boundary.

Migration policy locked in (Phase-43 / Prompt 0020 scope):
  • VehicleState.* fields → migrate to useUnits()/lib SI converters (range/speed/odometer/temp/charge_rate)
    Charger_power, power, time_to_full_charge are vendor-passthrough (kW, kW, hours) — keep literal display.
  • MotorSnapshot.{motor_temp_c_*, inverter_temp_c} → migrate to formatTemperature (°C input).
    power_kw / regen_kw / torque_nm_* / motor_rpm_* → keep literal kW/Nm/RPM display (already vendor-correct).
  • ClimateSnapshot.{*_temp_c} → migrate to formatTemperature.
  • TirePressureSnapshot.front_*/rear_* → Pa input. Migrate to formatPressure(kPa) with paToKpa(/1000) helper.
    tirePressureVariant() updated to take Pa input + Pa thresholds (single source of truth in helpers.ts).
  • Drive.distance_mi (RecentActivity / RecentDrivesSection / BatteryRangeCharts driveChartData) →
    KEEP useSettings().convertDistance — drive fields remain in legacy mi after SQL adapter rounds the SI →
    miles boundary. This is OUT of phase-43 scope; tracked for a future follow-up audit.
  • Position.speed_mph / LocationSnapshot.miles_to_arrival / ChargingTelemetry.charge_rate_mph etc. →
    KEEP existing display semantics. types.ts has NO "derived SI" comment on these fields; the prior phase
    plan (memory: phase-43 0013 / 0014) left them in their suffix-named display contract. A future audit
    must reconcile field-name vs underlying SI value for signal_log-projected Position/LocationSnapshot
    once the equivalent backend conversions are decided.
  • live.currentSpeedLimit (VehicleStatePanel SSE field) → SI m/s per CurrentLimitMph UnitKindDistance.
    Migrate to formatSpeed.

