=== NOTES ===
Locked policy (out-of-scope SI reconciliation):
- Drive.distance_mi / Drive.avg_speed_mph / Drive.max_speed_mph: SQL adapter
  in internal/database/drive_repo.go converts m->mi and m/s->mph BEFORE the
  HTTP layer, so these fields stay legacy. RecentDrivesSection.tsx,
  RecentActivity.tsx, and BatteryRangeCharts.tsx (Drive sections) keep
  useSettings/convertDistance.
- Position.speed_mph (VehicleCharts.tsx), LocationSnapshot.miles_to_arrival
  (MediaNavigationPanel.tsx), and ChargingTelemetry.charge_* fields
  (ChargingTelemetrySection.tsx) are misleadingly-named but carry SI values
  per the new backend. Per Phase-43 plan, full reconciliation is deferred to
  a follow-up audit prompt that will either rename the JSON fields or wrap
  with explicit SI->display conversion at the boundary. Touching them now
  would either ship visibly-wrong numbers OR require backend renames outside
  this prompt's allowed-files scope.

Gauge MAX constants (VehicleGauges.tsx): introduced explicit SI ceilings
- MAX_RANGE_METERS = 600 mi -> 965606 m
- MAX_SPEED_MPS = 250 km/h -> ~111.76 m/s
- MAX_CHARGE_RATE_METERS_PER_HOUR = 100 mi/h -> 160934.4 m/h
Pre-converted via convertDistanceFromSI / convertSpeedFromSI so the value
and max passed to RadialGauge / MetricBar share one display unit. Fixed a
dimensional bug where the old code used state.charger_power (kW) as the
ceiling for state.charge_rate (m/h after SI cutover).

Tire pressure (helpers.ts): single source of truth for thresholds in
TIRE_PRESSURE_PA frozen object (LOW_CRITICAL/LOW_WARNING/HIGH_WARNING/
HIGH_CRITICAL in Pascals). paToKpa(pa) helper handles the boundary because
useUnits.formatPressure expects kPa (matching lib/unitConversion's pressure
contract), but VehicleState/TirePressureSnapshot exposes Pa. Both
TirePressureSection and TirePressurePanel import from the helpers module to
avoid duplication.

Hooks: all 4 hooks (useVehicles, useVehicleSystems, useVehicleAccess,
useVehicleCommand) audited; their URLs are already prefix-correct (no
/api/v1/) and their return types already point at the regenerated
@/api/types interfaces from prompt 0011. Zero source edits required.

Gate script note: the prompt's verbatim audit regex uses backtick-double-
quote escapes (['\`""]) that fail to parse in PowerShell 7. Replaced with
semantically-equivalent regex using double-double-quote escapes ("[""']")
that PowerShell parses cleanly. Same character class ['"] in the actual
regex; same audit semantics. Also resolved the prompt's ${log} to
absolute path BEFORE Push-Location web (Phase-46/64 + Phase-46/99 known
fix) so Tee-Object inside web/ doesn't lose the log file.

Predecessor-log housekeeping: the working tree had two stray uncommitted
lines (=== COMMIT === + git rev-parse HEAD: ...) appended to
phase-43-0014-api-client-audit.log from a prior session. Reverted via
git checkout HEAD -- to restore committed state. Did not modify; not in
this prompt's scope.


